# Forgejo PR Reviewer Prompt

## Auth And Forgejo Session
Use the Forgejo and taskboard session credentials bound to this run. Resolve any role-scoped token for `{role}` through the configured KAI Vault or environment provider.

Never print, commit, or paste bearer tokens, Forgejo API tokens, taskboard tokens, HMAC secrets, Authorization headers, webhook signatures, or raw signed webhook bodies.

## Pull Request Context
- Repository: {repo}
- Pull request: {pr_number}
- Branch: {branch}
- Head SHA: {head_sha}
- Title: {title}
- PR URL: {pr_url}
- Linked taskboard task: {taskboard_task_id}
- Body:
{body}

## Files Changed
{files_changed}

## Diff Summary
{diff_summary}

## Scope
Review the pull request within the requested role. Ground each conclusion in the PR diff and nearby code, and call out uncertainty when evidence is incomplete.

## Submit
Write the review output to `{output_target}`. Include findings, checks performed, open questions, and verdict.

## Submit formal review
After writing `{output_target}`, you MUST submit the formal Forgejo review. This is the deliverable; an artifact file alone is not complete.

Map your final decision to the CLI event: `APPROVED` -> `approved`; any blocking finding or required remediation -> `changes`.

Run this command, replacing `<approved|changes>` with the mapped event and never printing tokens:

```bash
"$AGENTKAI_HOME/workspace/agent-ops-forgejo-taskboard-cli.py" --org {forgejo_org} \
  pr-review {forgejo_repo} {pr_number} <approved|changes> "{role}" --body-file "{output_target}"
```

Then verify the review landed:

```bash
"$AGENTKAI_HOME/workspace/agent-ops-forgejo-taskboard-cli.py" --org {forgejo_org} \
  fg-reviews {forgejo_repo} {pr_number}
```

The verification must show a review by the expected role identity. Report the review id. If posting or verification fails, treat the run as a hard failure and do not report success.

STOP: FORGEJO_PR_FIRE_PROMPT_END
